                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have had this game sitting in my library for a very long time, unplayed. I have always heard that it is a good game, and I have played a ton of [i]Salt and Sanctuary[/i], so I knew that the devs were able to make a great game, but for one reason or another, I just never quite got around to playing it. Now that I have played it, I'm mad at myself for putting it off for so long. I've been glued to it since starting.\n\nThis is a top notch beat 'em up game, although I would almost classify it as an action RPG, there is XP, equipment, and skills, and multiple classes to play as. On top of the great core gameplay, things get switched up once and a while with minigame segments. You get your \"surfing down a hill while fighting enemies\" levels, your shmup segments, and of course, your rhythm games. Very strong vibes of the good old beat 'em ups, a bit of TMNT, a dash of Shinobi III, even a smidge of Sunset Riders. I even got a slight Metal Slug feeling a few times, but my stongest feeling was \"this is like Battletoads, but actually beatable\". Very different theme and more depth, sure, but gameplay-wise... very Battletoads-esque with the varied gameplay.\n\nThere is a reason that this game has an overwhelmingly positive rating, and now I finally understand why. If you've played this game, then I'm preaching to the choir here, but if you are looking at this game knowing nothing about it, then know now that this is a great game that is worth playing. I should also mention that it has multiplayer, so if you can get some friends together, you can whoop some evil arse together in PVE, or each other's evil arses if PVP is your thing.",
